1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,033
Ask AI to write more tests?

2
00:00:02,033 --> 00:00:04,100
You probably don’t want to do that.

3
00:00:04,100 --> 00:00:08,733
In a large legacy system, tickets arrive faster than your team can close them.

4
00:00:08,733 --> 00:00:10,433
“Not enough automated tests!”

5
00:00:10,433 --> 00:00:11,967
You’re probably right.

6
00:00:11,967 --> 00:00:14,567
Tests define what your code should do: purpose.

7
00:00:14,567 --> 00:00:16,600
And show whether it does: proof.

8
00:00:16,600 --> 00:00:19,000
But first, they’re more code.

9
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:24,300
Test automation requires high-level software engineering—and must preserve the original intent.

10
00:00:24,300 --> 00:00:27,700
AI can pile on complexity before providing protection.

11
00:00:27,700 --> 00:00:28,633
Stop.

12
00:00:28,633 --> 00:00:29,667
And fix.

13
00:00:29,667 --> 00:00:31,367
Stop adding complexity.

14
00:00:31,367 --> 00:00:33,567
Get the system back under control.

15
00:00:33,567 --> 00:00:36,967
A better use of AI here? Hands-on testing.

16
00:00:36,967 --> 00:00:41,167
First, an isolated, repeatable environment that’s easy to set up.

17
00:00:41,167 --> 00:00:43,167
Show AI your manual checks.

18
00:00:43,167 --> 00:00:45,067
Have it perform similar tests:

19
00:00:45,067 --> 00:00:47,433
confirm fixes, explore for bugs,

20
00:00:47,433 --> 00:00:49,700
and check that known behavior still works.

21
00:00:49,700 --> 00:00:51,067
It’s a compromise.

22
00:00:51,067 --> 00:00:53,733
But a system already in panic needs relief—

23
00:00:53,733 --> 00:00:55,700
not more test code to maintain.

24
00:00:55,700 --> 00:00:59,533
Once you regain control, turn useful checks into test code.

25
00:00:59,533 --> 00:01:01,400
No AI needed to run it.

26
00:01:01,400 --> 00:01:04,133
For new features, express intent in tests first.

27
00:01:04,133 --> 00:01:05,667
Let them drive development.

28
00:01:05,667 --> 00:01:08,533
Then simplify. Delete redundant tests.

29
00:01:08,533 --> 00:01:10,933
Move suitable checks to fast unit tests.

30
00:01:10,933 --> 00:01:13,067
Keep essential end-to-end protection.

31
00:01:13,067 --> 00:01:15,733
Use spare AI to simplify and fix.

32
00:01:15,733 --> 00:01:19,933
Less to carry. Fewer bugs to chase.
